 Crows and the Horde through the outer tunnel; mmonster.co gives the outer gate for both."}},[16560]={["mapID"]=1416,["x"]=8.5,["y"]=59.2,["label"]="City Of Dalaran",["note"]="Forever. The Horde's way in: the sewer grate on Dalaran's western wall, by Lordamere Lake (players' guides give /way 8.8,59.6); warcraft.wiki.gg (https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/City_of_Dalaran) puts the instance line and summoning stone at 8,61. The client has no corpse point.",["evidence"]="https://github.com/Questie/QuestieDB/blob/36ca1ca86f6c1838de479c7c7452eb0a57d5c135/support/Forever/Zones/dungeons.lua#L143",["basis"]="Bundled entrance / reported",["alliance"]={["mapID"]=1416,["x"]=14.7,["y"]=63.0,["note"]="The Alliance's way in: the sewer pipe in Cantrips & Crows, inside the city (/way 14.68 62.99, on the Alterac Mountains map: the Cantrips & Crows NPCs Hexil Garrot and Shifty Vickers stand at 14.8,63.4 and 14.4,63.6 in QuestieDB's Forever data). wowforeverguides.com, wowclassicforever.info, wowforever.be and games.gg also put the Alliance in through Cantrips & Crows and the Horde through the outer tunnel; mmonster.co gives the outer gate for both."}},[16611]={["mapID"]=1420,["x"]=63.2,["y"]=67.5,["label"]="Ruins Of Lordaeron",["note"]="Forever. In the open ruins above the Undercity, near the way in from Brill (warcraft.wiki.gg, https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ruins_of_Lordaeron_(instance)). QuestieDB gives Undercity map 1458 72.48,11.33; the ruins are above ground, so the point is placed on Tirisfal Glades through both maps' Forever frames. The client has no corpse point.",["evidence"]="https://github.com/Questie/QuestieDB/blob/36ca1ca86f6c1838de479c7c7452eb0a57d5c135/support/Forever/Zones/dungeons.lua#L144",["basis"]="Bundled entrance / reported"},[16732]={["mapID"]=1437,["x"]=47.8,["y"]=56.2,["label"]="Excavation Site Wetlands",["note"]="Forever. Whelgar's Excavation Site; Forever's Highland Spider, Lurker and Tortoise (npcs.json 260803, 260804, 260809) are placed at 48-49,56-57 around i